<article class="env-definition" id="0DBW">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0DBW">Definition <span data-tag="0DBW">73.7.7</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme. Let $(\textit{Spaces}/S)_{fppf}$ be as in Definition <a href="/tag/0DBV" data-tag="0DBV">73.7.6</a>. Let $X$ be an algebraic space over $S$, i.e., an object of $(\textit{Spaces}/S)_{fppf}$. Then the big fppf site <em>$(\textit{Spaces}/X)_{fppf}$</em> of $X$ is the localization of the site $(\textit{Spaces}/S)_{fppf}$ at $X$ introduced in Sites, Section <a href="/tag/00XZ" data-tag="00XZ">7.25</a>. </p>
</article>